{"step_index":9467,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T08:33:37Z","thinking":"The user's browser, on their phone, is receiving a redirect from Google after authentication, which uses a local address. This results in the \"site can't be reached\" error, but the full URL, including an authorization code, is displayed in the address bar. The user is copying and pasting this URL, as they did previously. The code within the URL is likely the key to retrieving an access token.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request, urllib.parse\n\n# Test if feeding http://127.0.0.1:53682/?code=... works\n# Yes, rclone's internal web server handles GET /?state=...&code=...\nprint('Ready')\n\"","Cwd":"/home/azureuser","RequestedTerminalID":"","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Verifying oauth exchange script logic","toolSummary":"Check oauth logic"}}]}
